nodecode-ando is a rewrite of Ando-Corporation's Ando-Corporation/hermes-ando:

  https://github.com/Ando-Corporation/hermes-ando
  commit 1bfde877e1ed194ebf461d64e0468605d7e21a87

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ando Corporation (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the invitation flow (an invitation link accepted only for
the official Ando hosts, redeemed once, its key written to a mode-600 file),
the MCP client (initialize, tools/call and the server-sent answer, over
nlk:http instead of the MCP SDK), the inbox sweep over the direct and updates
scopes with its acknowledgement, the turn for each message and the reply
posted back to the conversation or its thread, and the "I stopped before I
could finish" notice. The original's Python, its Hermes gateway adapter and
its CLI are not bundled; the cell declares the same config as an `ando`
section.

What was left out, and why: the realtime WebSocket transport (a ticket and a
`ando.realtime.v1` socket, replaced by polling the durable inbox, which needs
no websocket dependency and loses nothing the inbox does not already keep);
file and voice attachments (upload, download and magic-byte typing, left for a
later pass so the first port stays text-only); Ando's per-member tool
preferences and the `disabled_tool_ids` filter; Hermes's OAuth MCP entry and
its scoped locks (the invitation's own api key replaces the OAuth sign-in);
and the original's Hermes-specific commands (`hermes ando connect/status/
doctor/receiving test`), which become the `/ando` command and the cell's
section here.
